      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the confirmation. Yes, `c2` above needs the intermediate cast to `uint16_t` to suppress the sign extension.\n\nFor `c1` above, it seems that we sign-extend it to `int`, cast it to `uint32_t`, left-shift it as `uint32_t` (so the sign-extended 1 bits, if any, are all shifted out), and then convert it to `uint64_t`. If my analysis is correct, this is very subtle.",
