      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I googled this question, I got the following AI Overview answer:\n\n```\nint16x4_t create_int16x4_t(int16_t val0, int16_t val1, int16_t val2, int16_t val3) {\n    int16x4_t result \u003d vdup_n_s16(0); // Initialize with zeros or any default value\n    result \u003d vsetq_lane_s16(val0, result, 0);\n    result \u003d vsetq_lane_s16(val1, result, 1);\n    result \u003d vsetq_lane_s16(val2, result, 2);\n    result \u003d vsetq_lane_s16(val3, result, 3);\n    return result;\n}\n```\n\nThere is a bug. After changing `vsetq` to `vset`, it seems to be correct and compiles to the same instructions as your version:\n\n```\nint16x4_t create_int16x4_t(int16_t val0, int16_t val1, int16_t val2, int16_t val3) {\n    int16x4_t result \u003d vdup_n_s16(0); // Initialize with zeros or any default value\n    result \u003d vset_lane_s16(val0, result, 0);\n    result \u003d vset_lane_s16(val1, result, 1);\n    result \u003d vset_lane_s16(val2, result, 2);\n    result \u003d vset_lane_s16(val3, result, 3);\n    return result;\n}\n```\n\nShould we switch to this version?",
